WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.299 --> 00:00:13.901
patrol officer made his rounds along a New York City street, twirling his baton.

2
00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:19.323
It was a little before 10 p.m., and a chilly wind had kept the streets empty.

3
00:00:20.683 --> 00:00:23.244
Halfway up a certain block, the officer slowed.

4
00:00:24.485 --> 00:00:29.067
In the doorway of a darkened hardware store, a man stood with his back against the door.

5
00:00:29.087 --> 00:00:31.788
"It's all right, Officer!"

6
00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:33.173
the man said quickly.

7
00:00:33.193 --> 00:00:35.995
"I'm just waiting here for a friend.

8
00:00:36.576 --> 00:00:39.818
Believe it or not, we made this appointment twenty years ago.

9
00:00:40.759 --> 00:00:47.264
You see, there used to be a restaurant where this store stands now—Big Joe Brady's."

10
00:00:48.305 --> 00:00:52.088
"Big Joe Brady's was torn down five years ago," the policeman said.

11
00:00:53.489 --> 00:00:57.512
The man stepped out from the doorway, peering both ways down the deserted street.

12
00:00:58.428 --> 00:01:05.093
A streetlight briefly lit him, revealing a pale, square-jawed face with sharp eyes and a noticeable white scar

13
00:01:05.173 --> 00:01:06.434
near his right eyebrow.

14
00:01:07.494 --> 00:01:09.936
His tie pin had a large, flashy diamond.

15
00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:18.482
"Twenty years ago tonight," the man went on, "I was here with my best friend, Jimmy Wells.

16
00:01:20.443 --> 00:01:26.187
I was eighteen and Jimmy was twenty, and the next morning, I was leaving to make my fortune

17
00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:26.867
out West."

18
00:01:29.461 --> 00:01:29.921
He chuckled.

19
00:01:29.941 --> 00:01:35.943
"But you couldn't have dragged Jimmy away—he thought New York was the only place on earth!"

20
00:01:37.064 --> 00:01:39.565
The policeman nodded as if he'd known people like that.

21
00:01:39.585 --> 00:01:47.048
"Well, that night we agreed to meet in this exact spot twenty years later.

22
00:01:48.128 --> 00:01:52.830
We figured that by then, we'd have each made our fortunes, whatever they were going to be."

23
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:57.972
"That's a long time between meetings," the officer said.

24
00:01:58.752 --> 00:02:00.414
"Have you heard from Jimmy since you left?"

25
00:02:01.575 --> 00:02:02.636
The man shook his head.

26
00:02:02.656 --> 00:02:09.262
"We wrote for a time, but we lost track of each other after a few years.

27
00:02:10.002 --> 00:02:13.125
The West is huge, and I moved around a lot.

28
00:02:14.186 --> 00:02:17.088
But Jimmy is the most dependable guy in the world.

29
00:02:17.789 --> 00:02:20.171
If he's still alive, he'll show up tonight."

30
00:02:21.693 --> 00:02:22.914
He pulled out a pocket watch.

31
00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:29.569
"It's almost ten—and it was exactly ten o'clock when we parted here twenty years ago."

32
00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.850
The policeman noticed that there were diamonds on the watch.

33
00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:37.151
"It looks like you've done well out West."

34
00:02:38.432 --> 00:02:40.912
"I have, and I hope Jimmy has done well too.

35
00:02:41.793 --> 00:02:45.794
Out West, I've had to compete with some very ambitious people."

36
00:02:47.094 --> 00:02:48.735
The policeman twirled his baton.

37
00:02:48.755 --> 00:02:50.455
"I'll be on my way now.

38
00:02:51.075 --> 00:02:52.436
I hope your friend shows up soon."

39
00:02:53.460 --> 00:02:55.981
"I'm sure he will, and I'll stick around until he does.

40
00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:57.002
Good night."

41
00:03:01.003 --> 00:03:03.084
The officer continued walking along his route.

42
00:03:04.245 --> 00:03:08.166
There was now a fine, cold drizzle falling, and the wind blew sharply.

43
00:03:09.247 --> 00:03:14.429
The few pedestrians in the streets hurried along, hands thrust in pockets and coat collars turned high.

44
00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:20.332
The man who had come a thousand miles to see his old friend continued waiting in the dark

45
00:03:20.372 --> 00:03:27.252
doorway. About twenty minutes later, a tall man in a long overcoat with its collar turned up stepped

46
00:03:27.292 --> 00:03:27.773
toward him.

47
00:03:27.793 --> 00:03:29.434
"Bob? Is that you?"

48
00:03:29.454 --> 00:03:31.196
"Jimmy Wells?"

49
00:03:32.356 --> 00:03:34.018
The tall man shook Bob's hand.

50
00:03:34.038 --> 00:03:37.481
"I was certain I'd find you here if you were still alive!

51
00:03:38.201 --> 00:03:39.782
How has the West treated you, old man?"

52
00:03:41.104 --> 00:03:42.965
"It's given me everything I hoped for!"

53
00:03:43.946 --> 00:03:46.648
Bob smiled and then eyed his friend up and down.

54
00:03:46.668 --> 00:03:51.312
"You've changed, Jimmy—you're taller now."

55
00:03:52.428 --> 00:03:54.349
"I grew a couple of inches in my twenties."

56
00:03:54.369 --> 00:03:57.450
"Are you doing well here in New York, Jimmy?"

57
00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:01.912
"I have a position in the municipal government," the tall man said.

58
00:04:01.932 --> 00:04:03.293
"Come on, Bob.

59
00:04:03.713 --> 00:04:06.274
Let's go to a place I know, so we can talk about old times."

60
00:04:08.555 --> 00:04:12.917
As the two men started walking, Bob boasted about his successful life out West.

61
00:04:13.517 --> 00:04:16.878
The other man, wrapped tightly in his overcoat, listened with interest.

62
00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:21.040
At the corner stood a brightly lit drugstore.

63
00:04:21.736 --> 00:04:24.638
Under the lights' glare, the two men turned to look at each other.

64
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:27.721
"You're not Jimmy Wells!"

65
00:04:28.081 --> 00:04:28.701
Bob snapped.

66
00:04:30.062 --> 00:04:35.006
"Twenty years is a long time, but not long enough to completely change the shape of a man's

67
00:04:35.106 --> 00:04:41.471
nose!" "But twenty years is enough time to change a good, decent man into a bad one," the

68
00:04:41.491 --> 00:04:42.211
tall man said.

69
00:04:42.231 --> 00:04:45.233
"You're under arrest, 'Sticky Fingers' Bob.

70
00:04:46.294 --> 00:04:48.636
The police in Chicago would like to have a chat with you."

71
00:04:50.336 --> 00:04:52.337
Bob was too stunned to say another word.

72
00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:56.239
"Before we go to the station, here's a note I was asked to hand you.

73
00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.661
It's from Officer Jimmy Wells."

74
00:04:59.561 --> 00:05:01.722
Bob unfolded the small slip of paper.

75
00:05:02.763 --> 00:05:06.725
His hand was steady when he began to read, but it was shaking by the time he had

76
00:05:06.785 --> 00:05:12.288
finished. Bob: I was at our meeting spot tonight at the agreed time.

77
00:05:13.069 --> 00:05:18.352
When you stepped into the light, I recognized the face of a notorious criminal who's wanted in Chicago.

78
00:05:19.286 --> 00:05:24.280
I couldn't bring myself to make the arrest, so I got a plainclothes officer to do the job.

79
00:05:24.982 --> 00:05:25.223
Jimmy
